g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Where P is the power of the source and r is the distance from the source.</p>\n<p><img alt=\"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift Physics - Electromagnetic Waves Question 4 English Explanation\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/6y3zli1mo5og5ql/f752ad78-ef3e-46d6-84f8-56afa048c465/206b0bd0-3be2-11f1-aafb-6f2b8ad54979/file-6y3zli1mo5og5qm.webp?format=webp\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1mo5og5ql/f752ad78-ef3e-46d6-84f8-56afa048c465/206b0bd0-3be2-11f1-aafb-6f2b8ad54979/file-6y3zli1mo5og5qm.webp\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/6y3zli1mo5og5ql/f752ad78-ef3e-46d6-84f8-56afa048c465/206b0bd0-3be2-11f1-aafb-6f2b8ad54979/file-6y3zli1mo5og5qm.webp?format=webp 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/6y3zli1mo5og5ql/f752ad78-ef3e-46d6-84f8-56afa048c465/206b0bd0-3be2-11f1-aafb-6f2b8ad54979/file-6y3zli1mo5og5qm.webp?format=webp 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/6y3zli1mo5og5ql/f752ad78-ef3e-46d6-84f8-56afa048c465/206b0bd0-3be2-11f1-aafb-6f2b8ad54979/file-6y3zli1mo5og5qm.webp?format=webp 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/6y3zli1mo5og5ql/f752ad78-ef3e-46d6-84f8-56afa048c465/206b0bd0-3be2-11f1-aafb-6f2b8ad54979/file-6y3zli1mo5og5qm.webp?format=webp 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/6y3zli1mo5og5ql/f752ad78-ef3e-46d6-84f8-56afa048c465/206b0bd0-3be2-11f1-aafb-6f2b8ad54979/file-6y3zli1mo5og5qm.webp?format=webp 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/6y3zli1mo5og5ql/f752ad78-ef3e-46d6-84f8-56afa048c465/206b0bd0-3be2-11f1-aafb-6f2b8ad54979/file-6y3zli1mo5og5qm.webp?format=webp 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Initial distance is L and the intensity recorded is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.804ex\" height=\"1.92ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 797.6 848.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(394,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>\n<p>It is given that the detector is shifted to another location on the same spherical surface.</p>\n<p>On a spherical surface is all points are at a constant distance r from the center (the source).</p>\n<p>Since the detector remains on the same spherical surface, its distance from the point source remains L .</p>\n<p>The angle ( <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.25ex\" height=\"1.674ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -718 1436.6 740\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1033,404.1) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> ) represents a change in direction, but not a change in distance r .</p>\n<p>As r is constant <mjx-container class=\"Ma